BT 1 0 0 1 0 75.2 Tm /F1 8.8 Tf 12 TL (CVE-2026-14266 \(CVSS 7.0\) is a heap-based buffer overflow in 7-Zip's XZ decoder \(MixCoder_Code in C/XzDec.c\): specially) Tj T* (crafted XZ chunked data is written past its allocated buffer, giving arbitrary code execution in the user's context when a victim) Tj T* (opens or extracts a malicious archive. It affects 7-Zip 21.07 through 26.01 and is fixed in 26.02 \(released 25 Jun; ZDI advisory) Tj T* (ZDI-26-444 published 15 Jul\). No public PoC or in-the-wild exploitation was observed as of 20 Jul, but the enormous install) Tj T* -0.073741 Tw (base and the routine use of archives as phishing attachments make this a high-value client-side RCE. 7-Zip has no auto-update) Tj T* 0 Tw (mechanism, so unmanaged installs stay vulnerable indefinitely - push 26.02 across the estate and check for) Tj T* (portable/standalone copies and bundled 7z binaries inside other tooling.) Tj T* ET
