BT 1 0 0 1 0 123.2 Tm /F1 8.8 Tf 12 TL (MemGhost is a memory-poisoning attack against inbox-reading AI assistants: a single crafted email rewrites what a persistent) Tj T* (agent 'remembers' about its user. Rather than a transient prompt injection, the poison is written to core context files) Tj T* (\(OpenClaw's plain-text AGENTS.md / MEMORY.md\) that load at the start of every session - so it survives context clears and) Tj T* (later steers unrelated tool calls, recipients or approvals. In the paper \(arXiv 2607.05189, 'When Claws Remember but Do Not) Tj T* (Tell'\), the one-shot payload framework achieves 87.5% end-to-end success against OpenClaw + GPT-5.4 and 71.4% against) Tj T* (the Claude Code SDK + Sonnet 4.6, transferring across agent architectures \(NanoClaw, Hermes Agent\) and filesystem/vector) Tj T* (\(Mem0\) memory backends, evaluated on the 108-case WhisperBench using a real IMAP/SMTP email workflow. No attachment) Tj T* (execution or link click is needed - the agent ingesting the message body is sufficient, and anyone who knows the victim's email) Tj T* (address can attempt it. Treat all agent-ingested content as untrusted data at the memory-write path \(not just at prompt) Tj T* (assembly\), require explicit user confirmation for memory writes derived from third-party content, and log/segment agent) Tj T* (memory by trust origin.) Tj T* ET
